From 46460d93aaaaa0788380559971d20b2f3dc72c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mario Behn <mario.behn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:01:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] iio_ws_proxy: port to the libiio 1.0 stream API

RX uses an iio_stream of eight blocks, one WebSocket frame per block;
the stream is dropped and recreated after an error and released when
the lazy mode has no client. TX streaming (four blocks) fills the current
block from the WebSocket and hands it over with the next
iio_stream_get_next_block. The cyclic mode (-l, used by the signal
generator) plays one cyclic block: the data is collected in a staging
buffer and a new push closes and reopens the buffer, because libiio 1.0
and the kernel refuse a second cyclic block (EBUSY). The 0.x version
wrote into the playing buffer and failed the second push with EBUSY.

Tested on Pluto+ against the 0.x build: RX frames identical in -1, all
channels, -C (size) and -L modes, TX stream tone correct, cyclic push of
a second tone replaces the first, full duplex at the real-time rate.

Signed-off-by: Mario Behn <mario.behn@gmail.com>
